f_midi: configfs options in_names / out_names, USB MIDI jack names (iJack) (lab only).

f_midi gives every jack iJack = 0, so snd-usb-audio on the host names the ports
"<product> MIDI 1".."N". With in_names / out_names (comma-separated, in port order) each named
port's embedded and external jack get a string descriptor of that name, and snd-usb-audio names
the port "<product> <name>" (or just <name> when it starts with the product name). The lab's
XL rear-MIDI gadget sets "MIDI In 1,MIDI In 2" and "MIDI In 1 / Out A,..,MIDI Out D" (the ALSA
sequencer names a port used both ways after its output; mpclab-midi-gadget). Unset (default):
no extra strings, iJack 0, the stock descriptors byte for byte. Applies on top of 0005, 0006.
